This iterates through the linked list. At each node, if the next node has the same value, it skips that node by linking the current node to the node after next. Otherwise, it moves to the next node. This has the effect of removing all duplicate nodes, leaving only one of each value.

Time complexity: O(N) since we iterate the list once. 
Space complexity: O(1) since we only use a constant number of pointers.

